; Companion to bug_018: a direct (non-generic) `.within
; cose.COSE_Encrypt0` from inside an imported library, where the
; `cose` namespace comes from the library's own import and the
; consumer does not import `cose` itself.  This shape must already
; lint cleanly (no E030); it pins the contrast with the bug-018
; generic case.
;
; The library file defines a plain rule `direct-encrypt` whose
; effective type uses `.within cose.COSE_Encrypt0`.  The consumer
; instantiates that plain rule through an `encrypt.` alias.

root = encrypt.direct-encrypt

;# import encrypt.direct-encrypt from "./support/bug_018_wrapper_lib_plain.cddl" as encrypt
